course: dictionary
lesson: 1912
title: Combatant and non-combatant
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A combatant is a person, army or country that takes part in fighting in a war or battle. Combat means fighting, so a combatant is someone who is in the fight.
explain: The word can also mean a person who takes part in a fight, argument or contest. Look at the words around it to see which meaning fits. In history books and news reports, it usually means someone fighting in a war.
explain: Combatant can also be an adjective, describing someone who is fighting. A non-combatant is the opposite: someone who is not fighting, such as a doctor or a civilian. The prefix non- means not, so you can work out this word from the parts you already know.
fact: Combatant means a person, army or country that takes part in fighting in a war or battle.
fact: A combatant can also be anyone who takes part in a fight, argument or contest.
fact: A non-combatant is someone who is not fighting, such as a doctor or a civilian.
fact: The phrase «enemy combatant» is used in formal and news language. In one country's law, it describes a prisoner who is denied the rights of a prisoner of war.
fact: Non- means not, so you can work out a new word by looking at its parts.
exercise: In history, what is a combatant? | *Someone who takes part in fighting in a war or battle | A church bell | A person who runs a shop in town | Someone who cooks food for the soldiers
exercise: A doctor who works in a war hospital is a non-combatant. What does non-combatant mean? | *A person who is not fighting | A country that wins every battle | A famous soldier | A person who fights in a war
exercise: Which word means the opposite of combatant when talking about war? | Enemy | Battle | Soldier | *Non-combatant
test: Which of these is a non-combatant in a war? | *A civilian who is not fighting | A soldier in a tank | A pilot in the air force | An army general leading troops
test: In a contest, who counts as a combatant? | The person who sells the tickets | Only the winner after the contest | *Anyone who takes part in the fight or contest | Only the referee
exam: What does combatant mean in its first meaning? | A shop that sells fighting gear | A person who watches the news | A quiet person who avoids all arguments | *A person, army or country that takes part in fighting in a war or battle
